# KP2 build pack — secrets only. Generated by scripts/gen-secrets.sh; never
# committed (.gitignore). Deployment shape lives in deployment.yaml.
#
# Do NOT copy this file by hand and do NOT invent values here:
#   scripts/gen-secrets.sh
# writes a .env with random, shell-safe values. The pack refuses to deploy
# while the placeholders below are still in place.
#
# This file is PARSED, never sourced (scripts/lib-core.sh's kp2_load_env --
# sourcing it would execute it, and join-api can write the tree it sits in).
# Practical differences from the old `set -a; . .env`: one layer of matching
# single or double quotes is stripped and the rest of the value is taken
# LITERALLY, so `$VAR` and `$(cmd)` inside a double-quoted value are no longer
# expanded; an unquoted value may not contain whitespace; and a line that is
# not KEY=VALUE is a refusal naming the line, not a silent skip.
XROAD_TOKEN_PIN=CHANGEME-run-scripts-gen-secrets.sh
XROAD_ADMIN_USER=xrd
XROAD_ADMIN_PASSWORD=CHANGEME-run-scripts-gen-secrets.sh
# KP2_JOIN_APPLICANT_TOKEN may also be set to the literal string "disabled"
# (not empty -- docker-compose.yml's :- default already passes an absent
# value through, so absence would silently mean "disabled" the moment this
# line was forgotten) -- the droplet target's posture, the switch
# deployment.yaml's posture: production pairs it with
# (join_workflow.enforce_ownership: true; docs/production-delta.md row 28,
# runbook.md's production-posture notes): the shared demo
# credential stops working outright and every applicant call must arrive on
# an issued per-agency credential instead (POST /tokens). The console is
# unaffected either way -- it never holds this token, only
# KP2_JOIN_OPERATOR_TOKEN, which can never be set to "disabled" this way.
KP2_JOIN_APPLICANT_TOKEN=CHANGEME-run-scripts-gen-secrets.sh
KP2_JOIN_OPERATOR_TOKEN=CHANGEME-run-scripts-gen-secrets.sh
# Only needed when deployment.yaml's datastore.kind: postgres. On the CI
# path this key (and _RO and KP2_DB_CA_CERT below) is written into the
# droplet's .env automatically by infra/ci/db-sync.sh on every up/deploy
# -- what follows is the laptop procedure. Unlike the
# secrets above, scripts/gen-secrets.sh does NOT generate this value -- the
# password is issued by DigitalOcean, not invented locally (run
# `terraform output -raw kp2_join_dsn_template` from infra/terraform-db/,
# see runbook.md's "The Postgres join store" section). Expected shape (quote
# it -- .env is shell-sourced and the DSN's `&` backgrounds the rest of an
# unquoted assignment, silently truncating the value):
# KP2_JOIN_DB_URL='postgresql://joinapi:PASSWORD@private-host:25060/kp2_join?sslmode=verify-full&sslrootcert=/pack-secrets/do-db-ca.crt'
KP2_JOIN_DB_URL=CHANGEME-postgres-dsn-see-runbook-the-postgres-join-store
# Optional: the read-only joinapi_ro role's DSN, same shape as
# KP2_JOIN_DB_URL above but with joinapi_ro's password (infra/terraform-db's
# `joinapi_ro_dsn_template` output). store.py's host-side `python -m store
# dump-records`/`check` use this for reads when it is set, falling back to
# KP2_JOIN_DB_URL otherwise -- `amend-refresh` always needs the read-write
# DSN and never looks at this one.
# KP2_JOIN_DB_URL_RO='postgresql://joinapi_ro:PASSWORD@private-host:25060/kp2_join?sslmode=verify-full&sslrootcert=/pack-secrets/do-db-ca.crt'
# Host path to the DigitalOcean cluster CA cert named in KP2_JOIN_DB_URL's
# sslrootcert above. Not a secret -- it is a public cert -- so this is a
# path, not a CHANGEME credential. Only needed for datastore.kind: postgres.
# KP2_DB_CA_CERT=/path/to/do-db-ca.crt
